course: dictionary
lesson: 12375
title: One word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cruise can change its job depending on the sentence. As a naming word it is a holiday on a ship, and as an action word it means to move at a steady pace. Context tells you which one is meant.
explain: «We went on a cruise around the islands.» Here cruise names a holiday on a big ship that visits several places. The clues are went on, islands and the idea of a holiday.
explain: «The plane cruised at 900 km/h.» Now cruise is an action. The plane flies at a steady, comfortable speed, and the number tells you that speed is the clue.
fact: Cruise can be a noun (a cruise) or a verb (to cruise).
fact: A cruise is a holiday on a large ship that visits several places.
fact: As a verb, cruise can mean to sail, drive or fly at a steady, comfortable speed.
fact: Informal: cruise can mean to win or do something very easily, as in «they cruised to victory».
fact: Useful phrases: cruise ship, cruising speed, cruise control, and cruise through (to do something easily).
exercise: «We booked a cruise for the summer holidays.» What is a cruise here? | A short walk in the park | A type of food | *A holiday on a large ship that visits several places | A fast race on a road
exercise: «The train cruised at a steady speed across the flat fields.» What does cruised mean? | *Moved at a steady, comfortable speed | Crashed into a fence | Whistled loudly | Stopped suddenly
exercise: «Our team cruised to victory, winning by ten goals.» What does cruised mean here? | To lose by a little | To sing a song after the game | *To win very easily | To run very slowly with tired legs
test: What does «cruising speed» mean? | A speed for racing | *A steady, comfortable speed | A speed for stopping suddenly | A speed for going backwards
test: A ship cruises at 10 km/h for 3 hours. How far does it go? Use distance = speed x time. | 300 km | 13 km | *30 km | 7 km
exam: Which sentence uses cruise to mean a holiday on a ship? | *«We went on a cruise around the islands.» | «They cruised to an easy win.» | «The car cruised down the motorway.» | «The fox cruised through the field looking for food.»
